1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,880
One goat died.

2
00:00:01,541 --> 00:00:02,321
One goat lived.

3
00:00:02,921 --> 00:00:03,441
Why two?

4
00:00:04,262 --> 00:00:06,042
I am Aaron, the high priest.

5
00:00:06,663 --> 00:00:09,504
I lived long before Jesus, so watch my goats.

6
00:00:10,064 --> 00:00:12,265
The first I killed, to pay for the people's

7
00:00:12,305 --> 00:00:12,605
sin.

8
00:00:13,365 --> 00:00:15,826
I carried its blood behind the curtain, where

9
00:00:15,866 --> 00:00:18,567
God's presence was, and no one else could go.

10
00:00:19,268 --> 00:00:20,528
The second I did not kill.

11
00:00:21,228 --> 00:00:23,669
I laid both hands on its head, and confessed

12
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:24,530
the people's sins.

13
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:28,131
Then it was sent away alive, into the wilderness.

14
00:00:29,652 --> 00:00:31,172
The dead goat could not walk away.

15
00:00:31,773 --> 00:00:33,193
The living goat could not pay.

16
00:00:33,894 --> 00:00:35,914
Jesus, God's Son, did both.

17
00:00:36,595 --> 00:00:39,116
He came to put away sin by the sacrifice of

18
00:00:39,156 --> 00:00:39,556
himself.

19
00:00:40,316 --> 00:00:42,977
When He died, the temple curtain tore, from

20
00:00:43,017 --> 00:00:44,058
the top to the bottom.

21
00:00:45,738 --> 00:00:47,359
I went in once a year, alone.

22
00:00:47,819 --> 00:00:49,480
Through Jesus, the curtain is open.

23
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:51,060
Walk through, to God.
